{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/174883-inspiration-for-heirs-to-hell-stories-spoilers","id":174883,"title":"Inspiration for Heirs to Hell stories (Spoilers?)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-19T20:22:52-07:00","id":174883,"title":"Inspiration for Heirs to Hell stories (Spoilers?)","content":"So I just finished the first season of this show Touch. The premise is Kiefer Sutherland plays the father to a child with a very special ability to recognize patterns of numbers with significance. The complication is that Jake, the child, doesn't talk and doesn't like to be touched. He's prone to strange behaviors which can endanger him, like climbing onto cellphone towers or running off when he's supposed to be relaxing. This is usually done to call attention to the numbers. Martin Bohm, Jake's father, follows these numbers into situations where he subtly affects peoples lives, helping them through problems and correcting &quot;imbalances&quot; in the universe. There's probably better summaries that can be Googled.<br /> <br /> I really like it, though I can see how the premise is a bit weird and why it got canned ultimately. Watching the season finale after reading Heirs to Hell, it occurred to me that the story of Jake and Martin struck me as a great Heirs to Hell kind of story. Maybe Jake's mother, who seems to have died in the 9/11 terrorist attacks, was a Demon? Martin is a regular Human and Jake is Offspring. It struck me that playing as Martin trying to protect his Offspring child from the machinations of Aster Corp (The Deva Corporation!) could make for a really neat game. Admittedly, I'm a sucker for parent-child narratives like this, where the protagonist have really earnest, human motivations like protecting children.<br /> <br /> Have you guys run into other stuff that might be cool <i>Heirs to Hell </i>inspiration? Do tell!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T21:58:28-07:00","id":174952,"title":"","content":"If you like light hearted fare:<br /> <br /> The Gallagher Girls Series<br /> Cloak and Dagger, a movie from 1984<br /> Welcome to Nightvale<br /> <br /> Persona 4 could easily be adapted to a group of young demonic children trying to rescue their schoolmates from hostile infrastructure.<br /> <br /> On a darker note...<br /> <br /> One of my teachers grew up behind the Iron Curtain during the height of Stalinism. Every day, before going to school, his parents would say &quot;be careful.&quot; Though they meant &quot;be careful what you say.&quot; Say the wrong thing, challenge the teacher or question communist doctrine and he'd come home to find his parents disappeared.<br /> <br /> The most recent Devil May Cry, despite being incredibly polarizing does deal with some of the challenges of growing up while being able see beyond the veil.<br /> <br /> Road to Perdition can be an excellent source, with the Mob being replaced by a corrupted Agency, Robbing backs being destroying infrastructure","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","user":"Agentwestmer","date":". 06-21-2014, 02:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T23:27:57-07:00","id":175015,"title":"","content":"Fringe is fantastic inspiration for anything God-Machine, but has some shenanigans involving a Splinter and a Latent. Anything further is mad spoilers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}